NAME
       exportfs - manage the list of directories an NFS server shares

SYNOPSIS
       exportfs -r
       exportfs -v

DESCRIPTION
       An NFS server shares (exports) the directories listed in /etc/exports
       and in files ending .exports in /etc/exports.d/. Each line names a
       directory, then the clients and their options:

           /exports/shared   192.168.50.0/24(rw,sync)

       exportfs makes the running NFS server use the list after you change
       it, and shows what is exported now. The server itself is the
       nfs-server service.

       On the RHCSA you are an NFS client: mount exports with mount -t nfs
       or autofs. This page is here to help you understand the other side.

OPTIONS
       -r     Re-export everything: read /etc/exports again.

       -v     Show what is exported, with the options.

       -a     Export everything in the lists.

EXAMPLES
           echo "/srv/share 192.168.50.0/24(rw)" >> /etc/exports
           exportfs -r
           exportfs -v

SEE ALSO
       exports(5), showmount(8), mount.nfs(8), nfs(5)
